From 89691701aa5417e092e17dd2d6f8c2a6353d2e97 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 01:41:22 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 272/404] Gui: the view follows what is looked at
 (TinkerCAD-like and touchpad navigation)

The wheel moves the eye towards the point of the model under the cursor (else
the point under the cursor at the focal depth) instead of zooming about a fixed
focal point: steps are proportional to the distance, slow down near the surface
and never pass it (the smallest distance keeps the point in front of Coin's
variable near plane); moving away has no limit. An orthographic camera zooms
about the same point by its height, as far as a perspective eye would come.

Turning is about the point of the model under the cursor; over the empty
background about the point last looked at while it is in the view, else the
middle of the model that is seen (a grid of picks), never a far away fixed
center. Moving grabs the point under the cursor. The wheel, moving and turning
bring the focal point to that depth, so the navigation cube turns about it;
fit all looks at the model's center. The pivot marker shows while turning.

Only the TinkerCAD-like (default) and touchpad styles (followsLook()); the
other styles are unchanged. The arithmetic is in LookNavigation.h with tests.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
